% Benchmark program: list construction and folding, exercised by
% `bench/scheme/bench/harness.sls` through the `list_sum` case.
%
% `range(N)` builds `[N-1, ..., 1, 0]` by recursion and `sum_list` folds
% it, so the case covers list spine matching, user-function dispatch and
% the `is` deep evaluator in one workload. The result is
% N*(N-1)/2: 124750 at N = 500, which is the value the harness checks.
%
% The `:- function range(int) -> list(int).` signature form matters: the
% bare `range(N) -> list(int).` is parsed as an equation whose body is a
% call to a `list` constructor, and `sum_list` then fails at run time
% with "no matching equation in lists:foldl_/3". Do not "simplify" it.
:- module(bench_list, [go/2]).

:- use_module(library(lists)).

:- chr_constraint go/2.

:- function range(int) -> list(int).

range(0) -> [].
range(N) -> [N - 1 | range(N - 1)].

go(N, R) <=> R is sum_list(range(N)).
